The diagram shows the curve $y = f(x)$, with the region between the curve and the $x$-axis over the interval shown shaded.
Which statement about the definite integral measuring that signed area is correct?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-1.2,0) -- (4.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3.6) -- (0,1.6) node[above] {$y$};
\fill[gray!35, domain=0:3, variable=\x] (0,0) -- plot ({\x},{0.32*(\x*\x - 9)}) -- (3,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick, <->, domain=-1:3.7, smooth, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.32*(\x*\x - 9)});
\node[above left] at (0,0) {$O$};
\node[above right] at (3,0) {$3$};
\node at (2.4,-2.4) {$y=f(x)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which definite integral gives the signed area of the shaded region shown?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[->] (-0.8,0) -- (3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-1.2) -- (0,6.0) node[above] {$y$};
\fill[gray!35] (1,0) -- (1,3) -- (2,1) -- (2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[thick, <->] (-0.4,5.8) -- (3.1,-1.2);
\draw[dashed] (1,0) -- (1,3);
\draw[dashed] (2,0) -- (2,1);
\node[below] at (1,0) {$1$};
\node[below] at (2,0) {$2$};
\node at (2.9,2.2) {$y=5-2x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
